From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:27:45 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 197/207] dsv41 server: TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE_DEFAULT runs
 compute in the engine for every chat

With the lane on, TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE_DEFAULT=1 reads every chat as
listing code_interpreter once, whatever the client sends: no tools, its
own function tools (they stay and their calls go back to it), a
code_interpreter of its own or a byte-equal copy of the built-in
definition (one declaration). tool_choice "none" hides the client's
tools but keeps the built-in one; a different function named python is
still refused. With the runner on, the boot's guide replaces a request's
runner_guide, and it is AB3's trust guide (53ed328f, 512 bytes) unless
TF_DSV41_RUNNER_GUIDE names another. The prompt equals an explicit
code_interpreter opt-in's.

Under the default every chat reply carries tensorfold.compute_executed:
calls (built-in calls run), runner_cells (cells the engine wrote) and
total, 0 when nothing ran. The flag without the lane, or any value but
unset, "", 0 and 1, stops the boot. Unset, nothing changes.
